---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import { business } from '../config/business';
const { founder } = business;
---

<Layout
  title="About Presence"
  description={`Presence Web Services is an independent business run by ${business.founder.name}, looking after websites and Google profiles with direct communication, agreed work and client-owned accounts.`}
>
  <PageIntro
    title="About Presence"
    description="An independent website and online presence service for businesses in Northern Ireland and across the UK."
  />

  <section
    class:list={['container', 'founder', { 'founder--with-photo': founder.photo }]}
    aria-labelledby="founder-heading"
  >
    <div class="founder-identity">
      {founder.photo && (
        <img
          class="founder-photo"
          src={founder.photo}
          alt={`${founder.name}, ${founder.role.toLowerCase()} of ${business.name}`}
          width={founder.photoWidth}
          height={founder.photoHeight}
          decoding="async"
        />
      )}
      <h2 id="founder-heading" class="section-title">
        Run by {founder.name}.
      </h2>
      <p class="founder-meta">
        {founder.role} · {founder.region}
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="founder-copy">
      <p class="lead">
        Most small business owners know their website could be doing more. Few have the time to work
        out what is holding it back, or much patience for a service that makes a few token edits
        each month and sends an automated report.
      </p>
      <p>
        {founder.name} started Presence to offer the alternative: one person who takes a genuine
        interest in your business and keeps improving how it shows up online. That starts with a
        conversation about which services you want more of, where your customers come from and what
        they need to know before they get in touch.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you work with Presence, {founder.name} is the person who reviews your website, does the
        work and replies to your emails.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
    <div class="container principles">
      <h2 id="principles-heading" class="section-title">
        How we work
      </h2>
      <dl class="principle-list">
        <div>
          <dt>You approve the priorities</dt>
          <dd>
            Every proposal sets out what’s included and what needs further assessment. You know your
            business best, so you decide which changes are worth making.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>You always know what changed</dt>
          <dd>
            Updates explain the work completed and what still needs attention. Where figures are
            available, we separate website activity from genuine enquiries and confirmed jobs.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Your accounts stay in your name</dt>
          <dd>
            You keep ownership of your website, domain and Google Business Profile. We use delegated
            access wherever the platform supports it.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>No promises we can’t keep</dt>
          <dd>
            Google decides its own rankings and customers decide whom to hire. We won’t guarantee
            either. We will tell you what we changed, why, and what the figures show afterwards.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container audience" aria-labelledby="audience-heading">
    <h2 id="audience-heading" class="section-title">
      Who we work with
    </h2>
    <div>
      <p class="lead">
        Trades, independent garages, landscapers, detailers, cleaning companies and other service
        businesses, in Belfast, across Northern Ireland and further afield in the UK.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can ask for help with an existing website, a new website or your Google business
        information.
      </p>
      <div class="scope-actions">
        <Button href="/contact/">Request a free audit</Button>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/services/">
          Explore the services
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
